{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>Save us</b> — One of the sages of Egypt said: This poet lived in the days of the Judges, before a king ruled over the children of Israel; therefore he says, \"and gather us from the nations.\" Another sage said: This poet was in Babylon. But the correct view in my eyes: This poet spoke in the Holy Spirit, and he speaks in the language of the children of our exile, \"Save us,\" just as Isaiah spoke in the language of the maskilim: \"Why do You lead us astray, YHWH, from Your ways\" (Isaiah 63:17)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 106, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:52.586185310Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}